  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Prepositions of Place \u2014 En, A, De",
      "content": "Spanish prepositions of place are essential for directions.\n\nEN = in, on, at (location)\n- El banco est\u00e1 EN la calle Mayor. (The bank is ON Mayor Street.)\n- Vivo EN Madrid. (I live IN Madrid.)\n\nA = to, at, near (direction/destination)\n- Voy A la estaci\u00f3n. (I'm going TO the station.)\n- Est\u00e1 A dos cuadras. (It's TWO blocks away.)\n\nDE = from, of (origin)\n- Soy DE Valencia. (I'm FROM Valencia.)\n- El museo ES DE esta ciudad. (The museum IS OF this city.)\n\nNear/Far:\n- cerca de (near)\n- lejos de (far from)\n- al lado de (next to)\n- entre (between)\n- enfrente de (in front of)\n- detr\u00e1s de (behind)",
      "examples": [
        "El hospital est\u00e1 en la calle Principal. (The hospital is on Main Street.)\nVoy a la estaci\u00f3n de metro. (I'm going to the metro station.)\n\u00bfEst\u00e1 lejos de aqu\u00ed? (Is it far from here?)",
        "El parque est\u00e1 entre el banco y la iglesia. (The park is between the bank and the church.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Imperative (Command) Form \u2014 Giving Directions",
      "content": "To give directions, you use the imperative (command) form.\n\nInformal (t\u00fa): Remove -r, add -a (AR verbs) or -e (ER/IR verbs)\n- Girar \u2192 GIRA a la derecha (Turn right)\n- Doblar \u2192 DOBLA a la izquierda (Turn left)\n- Seguir \u2192 SIGUE derecho (Go straight)\n\nFormal (usted): Add -e (AR verbs) or -a (ER/IR verbs)\n- Girar \u2192 GIRE a la derecha\n- Doblar \u2192 DOBLE a la izquierda\n\nCommon directional commands:\n- Siga derecho. (Go straight ahead \u2014 formal)\n- Gire a la derecha. (Turn right \u2014 formal)\n- Tome la primera calle. (Take the first street.)\n- Continue todo recto. (Keep going straight.)",
